<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Albanian Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1925 CE – 1928 CE · capital Tirana</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Albania's first republic, a presidential regime built by Ahmet Zogu that drew the country closely towards Fascist Italy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">Ahmet Zogu</a>, a chieftain from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mat-river">Mat</a>, was driven out by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fan-noli">Fan Noli's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/june-revolution-albania">June Revolution</a> of 1924 but returned in December with support from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia">Kingdom of Yugoslavia</a> and White Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>. In January 1925 a constituent assembly abolished the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-albania">Principality of Albania</a> and proclaimed a republic with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirana">Tirana</a> as capital, electing Zogu president for seven years.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The 1925 statute gave the president sweeping powers over the government, army and legislation. Zogu disarmed clans, suppressed opponents and built roads and a gendarmerie. Short of money, he turned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>: an Italian-controlled national bank and development company were founded, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-tirana">Treaties of Tirana</a> of 1926 and 1927 made <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> an Italian ally.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>On 1 September 1928 a constituent assembly proclaimed <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> a monarchy, and Zogu became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">King Zog</a> I of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albanian-kingdom">Albanian Kingdom</a>. The new constitution kept much of the presidential system but made the office hereditary, and the dependence on Italian money continued.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/albanian-republic.jpg" alt="Albanian Republic" width="320" height="229"><figcaption>Image: Sadik Kaceli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Albania.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1925 CE – 1928 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tirana</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ahmet Zogu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam, Orthodox and Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Albanian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/albania">Albania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>First Albanian Republic, Albanian Republic (1925-1928)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=albanian-republic" aria-label="Albanian Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5164 704 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Albanian Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5484 960L5475 960M5484 960L5484 960"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5475 960h0M5484 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5484 960h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5484 960h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tirana. <a href="/atlas?year=1926&amp;focus=albanian-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
